        <p>Koirala, B., &amp; Baptiste, D.-L. (2026). Just stats: T tests, analysis of variance tests, and nonparametric equivalents. <i>Journal for Nurse Practitioners, 22</i>(3), Article 105692. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nurpra.2026.105692</p>
        <p>U.S. Department of Health and Human Services, Office for Human Research Protections. (n.d.). <i>Quality improvement activities frequently asked questions.</i> Retrieved June 8, 2026, from https://www.hhs.gov/ohrp/regulations-and-policy/guidance/faq/quality-improvement-activities/index.html</p>
        <p>Winckler, B., McKenzie, S., &amp; Lo, H.-Y. (2024). A practical guide to QI data analysis: Run and statistical process control charts. <i>Hospital Pediatrics, 14</i>(1), e83-e89. https://doi.org/10.1542/hpeds.2023-007296</p>
        <p>Yoon, E., Tharakan, A., Johnson, C., Metz, C., &amp; Granger, B. B. (2025). Statistical process control charts to improve health care: Hypertension case. <i>AACN Advanced Critical Care, 36</i>(2), 197-204. https://doi.org/10.4037/aacnacc2025608</p>
        <p style="text-indent:0;padding-left:0;font-size:13.5px;border-top:1px dashed var(--line);padding-top:12px">Regulatory definition of research referenced throughout: 45 CFR 46.102. DOIs above were verified at the time of creation. Confirm access and currency before citing them in your paper.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>

